docs {
  # Registry WG demo

  This authorized local journey shows one standard registry interface over two
  different sources. The DHIS2-backed Adapter reads live public-demo data only.
  Create and conditional Update go only to the retained local BReg registry.
  The loopback issuer and its bearer token are synthetic demo infrastructure.

  Run all 13 requests in their saved order with the `LocalExample` environment:

  1. obtain a runtime-only demo token;
  2. List a live DHIS2 page and select its record and organisation unit;
  3. Retrieve the public `people` view, then Lookup and Search `people-summary`;
  4. Create a local BReg contact and prove exact Create replay;
  5. read its ETag, apply and replay a conditional merge patch that removes
     `note`, then read the resulting state;
  6. prove a stale `If-Match` returns 412 and leaves that state unchanged.

  Deployment-specific local contracts:

  - [DHIS2 Consultation](https://127.0.0.1:19443/contracts/dhis2/1.0.0/openapi.json)
  - [BReg Consultation and Write](https://127.0.0.1:19443/contracts/breg/1.0.0/openapi.json)

  The contract endpoint uses a demo-scoped self-signed certificate. This
  collection makes no DHIS2 Write, production-suitability, or general GovStack
  conformance claim. It stores no authentication configuration or token.
}
